From b9c6f3b1e186dc944719ea2b7c1dd57991c0fe66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:03:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cm): numerical ChiMerge honours alpha; Chi2 phases undo
 on inconsistency (audit X-04, A-05, A-08)

- OBN_CM: fit() merged the pre-bins down to max_bins before chi_merge(),
  whose loop then stopped at max_bins, so chi_merge_threshold never decided
  anything (alpha 0.5 / 0.05 / 0.001 gave identical bins, iterations = 0).
  The pre-enforce is removed and chi_merge() is Kerber's loop: merge the
  smallest chi-square pair while it is below the critical value OR more than
  max_bins bins remain, never below min_bins (max_bins is a ceiling). The
  |delta total IV| < tol stop (A-13b) is removed with it; `converged` is false
  only when max_iterations cuts the loop.
- Chi2 (numerical and categorical): phases at decreasing alpha; after each
  phase the inconsistency rate is measured and, when it exceeds that of the
  initial bins (Liu & Setiono's delta), the phase is undone and the algorithm
  stops; max_bins is applied afterwards. The old loops never ran a phase past
  alpha = 0.5 and stopped on a LOW inconsistency (inverted rule).
- Docs (roxygen + man) of ob_numerical_cm/ob_categorical_cm describe the
  new rules; test-cm-significance.R encoded the defect and is updated with a
  comment citing A-05; new regression tests in test-forensic-fixes-G1.R.
- audit/diffs/13: manifest + gate report (PASS; 4212/4212 non-target runs
  bit-identical). Merging non-significant bins lowers training and hold-out
  IV by construction (IV is monotone under refinement); the declared
  families are documented with hold-out log-loss evidence in the report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Vec7ZYQbZ1gRRpELoJZarP
