+pr: "G1-13: numerical ChiMerge honours alpha (Kerber); Chi2 phases with reversion (X-04 / A-05, A-08)"
+findings: [X-04, A-05, A-08]
+# Common theory for every ob_numerical_cm entry below. ChiMerge (Kerber 1992)
+# merges the adjacent pair with the smallest chi-square while it is below the
+# critical value of alpha OR while more than max_bins bins remain, never below
+# min_bins. The baseline merged the pre-bins down to max_bins and stopped, so
+# (with the pure-bin rule of manifest 10 held fixed) the merge sequence of the
+# candidate is the SAME greedy smallest-chi-square sequence, continued until
+# every pair differs significantly or min_bins binds: before the rare-bin and
+# monotonicity passes the candidate partition is a coarsening of the former
+# one. IV (training or hold-out, any sample) never increases under
+# coarsening (data-processing inequality / log-sum inequality), so a lower IV
+# is the expected, intended effect of honouring alpha and cannot by itself
+# show a regression. Supplementary hold-out evidence that is not biased toward
+# more bins -- the mean hold-out log-loss of the binned event-rate model
+# (train-bin rates, Jeffreys-smoothed) -- is quoted per entry; over all 180
+# ob_numerical_cm runs it improves from 0.4790 to 0.4440.
+targets:
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "imbalance/rate_1pct/*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      About 21 events in 2100 training rows (expected cell counts below 5 in
+      most 2x2 tables). Adjacent baseline bins such as 4/416 vs 8/412 events
+      (s1) are not significantly different at alpha = 0.05, so Kerber merges
+      them (s1 5 -> 3 bins, s2 4 -> 3, s3 4 -> 3, min_bins = 3). The hold-out
+      IV median falls 1.93 -> 1.56 (default/wide) and 1.56 -> 1.33 (tight) by
+      the coarsening argument above; with ~9 hold-out events it is dominated by
+      sampling noise. Hold-out log-loss changes by +0.0010 / +0.0019 / +0.0012
+      nats (default / tight / wide, on 0.058).
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "imbalance/rate_02pct/*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: "any"
+      nonmono: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      About 4 events in 2100 training rows. The baseline also violated
+      min_bins here (1-2 bins, see manifest 10); the candidate returns
+      min_bins = 3 bins, whose 1 / 1 / 0 events cannot be monotone, and
+      monotonicity merging stops at min_bins as documented. Hold-out IV with
+      ~1-2 test events is noise (tight 0.48 -> 0.06); hold-out log-loss is
+      unchanged or better (tight -0.00004 nats).
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "signal/step/*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: "any"
+      nonmono: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      The true rate has two levels (0.1 / 0.4 at x = 0.5). Kerber merges the
+      non-significant pieces (s2 tight: a 105-row bin at 32/73 events next to
+      a 945-row bin at 380/565 merges into the 2-bin step), lowering hold-out
+      IV 0.703 -> 0.670 by coarsening; log-loss +0.0009 nats on 0.50. With
+      min_bins = 3 (default/wide) the third bin must split one flat level of
+      the step, its WoE order is noise, and monotonicity merging stops at
+      min_bins (documented), hence the non-monotone runs.
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "discrete/ties/*"
+    params: "wide"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      round(rnorm, 1) with a weak logistic signal: the pre-bins that are not
+      significantly different at alpha = 0.05 are merged down from up to
+      8 bins; hold-out IV median 0.773 -> 0.722 by coarsening, hold-out
+      log-loss +0.0028 nats on 0.605 (0.5%).
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "scale/*"
+    params: "wide"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      scale/tiny and scale/huge are the same logistic (slope 1 on the
+      standardised value) at scales 1e-12 / 1e12; both give identical bins.
+      With max_bins = 8 Kerber merges the adjacent pre-bins whose rates do not
+      differ at alpha = 0.05 (smooth logistic: neighbouring quantile bins
+      differ little), hold-out IV median 0.743 -> 0.718 by coarsening;
+      hold-out log-loss +0.0024 nats on 0.608 (0.4%).
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "signal/u_shape/*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: ">="
+      nonmono: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      The true rate is U-shaped (0.6 / 0.1 / 0.6), so a correct binning is
+      non-monotone. Honouring alpha lets the significant tails survive (s1
+      wide: ref IV 0.46 -> 1.47; hold-out log-loss -0.042 nats).
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "signal/noise/*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: "any"
+      nonmono: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      No signal (true IV = 0, layer E skips the family): nothing is
+      significant, Kerber merges down to min_bins and the remaining WoE order
+      of min_bins = 3 noise bins is arbitrary.
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "size/small_n40/*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: ">="
+      nonmono: "any"
+    rationale: >
+      n = 40 (28 training rows): few pairs are significant, Kerber merges down
+      to min_bins = 3 and their WoE order is driven by 2-3 events per bin;
+      monotonicity merging stops at min_bins (documented). Hold-out log-loss
+      improves (wide -0.008 nats).
+  - engine: ob_numerical_cm
+    scenarios: "*"
+    expect:
+      ref_iv: "any"
+      oos_iv: ">="
+    rationale: >
+      See the common theory above: merging the pairs that are not
+      significantly different lowers training IV by construction.
+  # ob_categorical_cm: only its Chi2 path (use_chi2_algorithm = TRUE) changes
+  # here, which the corpus does not run; its default path is covered by
+  # manifest 11 (cumulative scope).
+non_targets: "bit-identical"
+breaking_change_note: >
+  ob_numerical_cm() now runs Kerber's ChiMerge: pairs that do not differ
+  significantly at chi_merge_threshold are merged down to min_bins and
+  max_bins is only a ceiling (the level used to have no effect). The Chi2
+  variant (numerical and categorical) runs its decreasing levels and undoes
+  and stops at the first level that raises the inconsistency rate.
